## Installation

Erlang with Rebar3:

```erlang
{deps, [{libdecaf, "3.0.0"}]}.
```

Elixir:

```elixir
defp deps do
  [{:libdecaf, "~> 3.0"}]
end
```

For erlang.mk, add `libdecaf` to `DEPS` and set
`dep_libdecaf = hex 3.0.0`.

Building requires Erlang/OTP 28 or later, GNU Make 4 or later, a C/C++ toolchain
with C23/C++20 support, CMake 3.22 or later, and Python 3. CI covers the latest
OTP 28 and OTP 29. The native dependency is included in the package.

## Quick start

Erlang:

```erlang
{ok, _} = libdecaf:start(),
Digest = libdecaf:hash(sha3_256, <<"abc">>),
<<"~J< erlang("{ok, _} = libdecaf:start(),\nDigest = libdecaf:hash(sha3_256, <<\"abc\">>),\nDigest", "hex") >.">> = binary:encode_hex(Digest),
Token = libdecaf:strong_rand_bytes(32).
```

Elixir calls the same Erlang API:

```elixir
{:ok, _} = :libdecaf.start()
digest = :libdecaf.hash(:sha3_256, "abc")
token = :libdecaf.strong_rand_bytes(32)
```

## Signatures and key agreement

Generate an Ed25519 keypair, sign a message, and verify it:

```erlang
Keypair = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair(ed25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),
PublicKey = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair_extract_public_key(Keypair),
% ~J< erlang("Keypair = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair(ed25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nPublicKey = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair_extract_public_key(Keypair),\nPublicKey") >.
Signature = libdecaf:eddsa_sign({ed25519, Keypair}, <<"message">>),
% ~J< erlang("Keypair = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair(ed25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nPublicKey = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair_extract_public_key(Keypair),\nSignature = libdecaf:eddsa_sign({ed25519, Keypair}, <<\"message\">>),\nSignature") >.
true = libdecaf:eddsa_verify({ed25519, PublicKey}, Signature, <<"message">>).
```

Ed25519ctx, Ed25519ph, Ed448, and Ed448ph accept an optional context in the
parameter tuple. Ed25519ph and Ed448ph also support streaming:

```erlang
Keypair = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair(ed448, binary:copy(<<7>>, 57)),
S0 = libdecaf:eddsa_sign_init({ed448ph, Keypair, <<"protocol/v1">>}),
S1 = libdecaf:eddsa_sign_update(S0, [<<"hello ">>, <<"world">>]),
Signature = libdecaf:eddsa_sign_final(S1),
% ~J< erlang("Keypair = libdecaf:eddsa_keypair(ed448, binary:copy(<<7>>, 57)),\nS0 = libdecaf:eddsa_sign_init({ed448ph, Keypair, <<\"protocol/v1\">>}),\nS1 = libdecaf:eddsa_sign_update(S0, [<<\"hello \">>, <<\"world\">>]),\nSignature = libdecaf:eddsa_sign_final(S1),\nSignature") >.
V0 = libdecaf:eddsa_verify_init({ed448ph, Keypair, <<"protocol/v1">>}, Signature),
V1 = libdecaf:eddsa_verify_update(V0, <<"hello world">>),
true = libdecaf:eddsa_verify_final(V1).
```

Pass original message bytes; the prehash is computed internally.

For X25519 or X448 key agreement:

```erlang
Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),
Bob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),
Shared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Alice, Bob),
% ~J< erlang("Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nBob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Alice, Bob),\nShared") >.
Shared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Bob, Alice).
% ~J< erlang("Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nBob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Alice, Bob),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Bob, Alice),\nShared") >.
```

Shared secrets are raw bytes for your protocol's key derivation. A rejected
peer key returns `error`. For curve-specific operations and encoded-key APIs,
see `libdecaf_curve25519` and `libdecaf_curve448`.

## Hashes, authentication tags, and XOFs

Choose the algorithm and options when initializing a stream. Keep each returned
state; states are immutable and can be reused to branch a computation. Input
accepts iodata, and all lengths are in **bytes**.

```erlang
H0 = libdecaf:hash_init(sha3_256),
H1 = libdecaf:hash_update(H0, <<"hello ">>),
H2 = libdecaf:hash_update(H1, <<"world">>),
Digest = libdecaf:hash_final(H2),
Digest = libdecaf:hash(sha3_256, <<"hello world">>).
```

KMAC and HopMAC take a key and optional customization string:

```erlang
Key = libdecaf:strong_rand_bytes(32),
Tag = libdecaf:hash({kmac128, 32, Key, <<"orders/v1">>}, <<"invoice-42">>).
```

XOFs let you read as much output as needed. Once squeezing starts, the returned
state can keep squeezing but cannot absorb more input:

```erlang
X0 = libdecaf:xof_init(shake128),
X1 = libdecaf:xof_absorb(X0, <<"abc">>),
{X2, First} = libdecaf:xof_squeeze(X1, 16),
{_X3, Second} = libdecaf:xof_squeeze(X2, 16),
Output = <<First/binary, Second/binary>>,
Output = libdecaf:xof(shake128, <<"abc">>, 32).
```

KT, HopMAC, and ParallelHash can use the parallel APIs for large inputs:

```erlang
Input = binary:copy(<<"abc">>, 10000),
Digest = libdecaf:parallel_hash(kt128, Input),
Digest = libdecaf:hash(kt128, Input).
```

The parallel streaming APIs are `parallel_hash_init/1`,
`parallel_hash_update/2`, `parallel_hash_final/1`, and the corresponding
`parallel_xof_init/1`, `parallel_xof_absorb/2`, `parallel_xof_squeeze/2` functions.
They produce the same output as the ordinary APIs.

See the [Hash and XOF guide](guides/hash-and-xof.md) for parameter forms,
TupleHash element boundaries, customization, and parallel configuration.

## Specialized modules

`libdecaf_ristretto255` and `libdecaf_decaf448` provide prime-order group arithmetic.
`libdecaf_tuak` exposes TUAK authentication and key generation. Use
`libdecaf:strong_rand_bytes/1` for automatically seeded random bytes, or
`libdecaf_spongerng` for explicit seeded streams.

Implementations are checked against published vectors from RFCs
[7748](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7748.html),
[8032](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032.html),
[9496](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9496.html), and
[9861](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9861.html), NIST
[FIPS 180-4](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/180-4/upd1/final),
[FIPS 202](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/202/final),
[SP 800-185](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/185/final), and 3GPP TUAK conformance data.

## Benchmark highlights

Bulk throughput on an Apple M3 Max with 14 schedulers, OTP 29,
and the ARM SHA3 backend. The parallel APIs reach **41 GB/s for KT128** and
**21 GB/s for ParallelHash128**, about **17×** and **18×** their ordinary APIs:

| Algorithm | Ordinary API | Parallel API | Speedup |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| TurboSHAKE128 | 2.5 GB/s | — | — |
| HopMAC128 | 2.4 GB/s | 41 GB/s | 17× |
| KT128 | 2.4 GB/s | 41 GB/s | 17× |
| KT256 | 2.0 GB/s | 31 GB/s | 16× |
| TurboSHAKE256 | 2.0 GB/s | — | — |
| HopMAC256 | 1.9 GB/s | 31 GB/s | 16× |
| cSHAKE128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| Keccak-XOF-128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| KMAC128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| KMACXOF128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| ParallelHash128 | 1.2 GB/s | 21 GB/s | 18× |
| ParallelHashXOF128 | 1.2 GB/s | 20 GB/s | 17× |
| SHAKE128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| TupleHash128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| TupleHashXOF128 | 1.2 GB/s | — | — |
| cSHAKE256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| Keccak-224 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| Keccak-256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| Keccak-XOF-256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| KMAC256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| KMACXOF256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| ParallelHashXOF256 | 1.0 GB/s | 16 GB/s | 17× |
| SHA3-224 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| SHA3-256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| SHAKE256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| TupleHash256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| TupleHashXOF256 | 1.0 GB/s | — | — |
| ParallelHash256 | 0.9 GB/s | 16 GB/s | 17× |
| Keccak-384 | 0.8 GB/s | — | — |
| SHA3-384 | 0.8 GB/s | — | — |
| SHA2-512 | 0.7 GB/s | — | — |
| Keccak-512 | 0.5 GB/s | — | — |
| SHA3-512 | 0.5 GB/s | — | — |

Five warmed streaming passes, including initialization and finalization,
with reused 64 MiB updates. Ordinary messages are 1 GiB; parallel messages are
32 GiB to measure sustained worker-pool throughput. ParallelHash uses 8 KiB blocks;
workers drain their queues until idle. Rates use decimal GB/s. Speedups use the unrounded measurements.
KMACXOF128, KMACXOF256, TupleHashXOF128, TupleHashXOF256, ParallelHashXOF128,
and ParallelHashXOF256 use the XOF API; other rows use the Hash API. Small messages favor the ordinary API.

[Full measurements and methodology](https://github.com/potatosalad/erlang-libdecaf/blob/main/bench/hash_highlights.md)
and [parallel size sweeps and native baselines](https://github.com/potatosalad/erlang-libdecaf/blob/main/bench/parallel_hash.md)
are available for comparison.

## Building, testing, and documentation

```sh
gmake
gmake tests
gmake lint
gmake docs
```

ExDoc writes the API reference and guides to `doc/index.html`, including source
links for release `3.0.0`. `rebar3 ex_doc` builds the same documentation directly.

Use `gmake format` after editing C or Erlang sources. Generated files are
maintained through `just codegen`. [Development](guides/development.md) covers
code generation, selected test suites, sanitizers, and package checks.

## Usage

Each example is independent and can be pasted into an Erlang shell.

### ECDH

<a id="example-x25519"></a>

#### X25519

Generate two keypairs and derive the same shared secret from either side:

```erlang
Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),
Bob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),
{AlicePK, AliceSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Alice),
{BobPK, BobSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Bob),
Shared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, AliceSK, BobPK),
% ~J< erlang("Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nBob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),\n{AlicePK, AliceSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Alice),\n{BobPK, BobSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Bob),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, AliceSK, BobPK),\nShared") >.
Shared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, BobSK, AlicePK),
% ~J< erlang("Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nBob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),\n{AlicePK, AliceSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Alice),\n{BobPK, BobSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Bob),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, AliceSK, BobPK),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, BobSK, AlicePK),\nShared") >.
Shared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Alice, Bob).
% ~J< erlang("Alice = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<7>>, 32)),\nBob = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair(x25519, binary:copy(<<19>>, 32)),\n{AlicePK, AliceSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Alice),\n{BobPK, BobSK} = libdecaf:ecdh_keypair_extract(Bob),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, AliceSK, BobPK),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, BobSK, AlicePK),\nShared = libdecaf:ecdh_shared_secret(x25519, Alice, Bob),\nShared") >.
```

